#
# Quarry, research: layer 69 of the matrix. A topic is searched for in the
# Hoard (search.query), a hit's text is read for its excerpt (files.read)
# and the owner's Web4 feed is read for signed envelopes (web4.feed); what
# the owner chooses is held as a numbered citation under its topic. The
# owner writes claims that each name a citation, and asks the companion
# (swarm.ask) for a summary of one topic's citations that cites them by
# number. Advisory and owner-confirmed: the summary is held until the
# owner accepts it (zxm.h M3), a bracketed number in it that names no
# citation of the topic is counted and shown, and a citation is dropped
# only on the owner's confirmed word.
#
# zxvd has no method to search the web, so Quarry searches only the Hoard
# and the Web4 feed; none is invented. An envelope marked pii is listed
# but never cited (the default taken: personal data stays out of a
# summary sent to the companion).
#
# Built on what is nearer the core. How many citations a topic holds,
# and how many carry one number, are witness's kind_count (KRON witnessed
# by Trebago) over the citations' topic and number columns, used as it
# is: the task's "sources per topic in KRON + Trebago" is that rule. The
# three new entries are general (any layer that writes claims, asks for
# a summary or keeps citations), so they are concepts in CONCEPTS.tsv
# with Quarry as owner.
#
# Witness pairs are of one kind: claim_sourced is a truth whose two
# fields each have their own range, Eve's (as the task asks), witnessed
# by KRON, which reads any positive held count as held where Eve takes
# exactly one: two citations under one number are held (BOTH) for the
# owner, never settled by a machine. The summary's length limits are
# Eve's and the citation record MYRA's, as the task asks.
#
# Kept in C, since no runnable language owns it: text work (an excerpt
# cut on a character boundary, the prompt laid out, the bracketed numbers
# and words of an answer counted) and reading zxvd's answers.
#
# Planned languages: dBase (records, query) waits for a runtime and takes
# the citation record (pending below). Python already has a runtime
# (python) and owns scripting and ai; Quarry has no entry of that kind
# (the summary is the companion's, through swarm.ask), so no pending line.
zxapp 1
id     quarry
name   Quarry
version 1.0.0
slot   69
layer  L1
matrix 69
icon   icons/l1/069-quarry.svg
budget 233
needs  search
needs  fs.read
needs  ai.ask
needs  net
model  apps/quarry_model.c
use    witness 1      # @num.witness_kind_count

# This claim has a source (QR1): cite 1..9999 carried by exactly one held
# citation (held, witness.kind_count over the numbers). Eve, witnessed by
# KRON.
provides claim_sourced truth cite held
logic    eve  claim_sourced apps/blocks/quarry/claim.eve
logic    kron claim_sourced apps/blocks/quarry/claim.kron

# A summary's length limits (QR2): 25..500 words from 1..32 sources. Eve.
provides summary_length_ok truth words sources
logic    eve summary_length_ok apps/blocks/quarry/summary.eve

# The citation record (QR3), a ^ZXQUARRY record in MYRA.
provides cite_record_ok truth cite topic kind stamp quote
logic    myra cite_record_ok apps/blocks/quarry/cite.myra
pending  dBase cite_record_ok

# Its own proof (zxapp.h K1): each entry at its edges, and where its languages disagree
check claim_sourced cite=1,9999,0,10000,5,5,-1 held=1,1,1,1,0,1,1 = true,true,false,false,false,true,false
check claim_sourced cite=5,5 held=1,2 = both
check claim_sourced cite=5,5 held=1,3 = both
check summary_length_ok words=25,500,24,501,100,100,100 sources=1,32,1,1,0,33,-1 = true,true,false,false,false,false,false
check cite_record_ok cite=1,9999,10000,1,1,1,1,-9999 topic=1,999,1,1000,1,1,1,1 kind=1,9,1,1,10,1,1,1 stamp=1760000000,999999999999,1,1,1,1000000000000,1,1 quote=0,99999,0,0,0,0,100000,0 = true,true,false,false,false,false,false,true
# Sources per topic: the citations of topic 1 among five, and the citations carrying number 7
check witness.kind_count kind=1,2,2,1,1 want=1 = 3
check witness.kind_count kind=3,7,9 want=7 = 1
